vulnerabilities.suggested_fix:
In `_checkSolvencyAtTicks`, when `safeMode > 0`, apply the conservative utilization override to *every* entry in `positionBalanceArray`, not just `[0]`.

Example:
```solidity
if (safeMode > 0) {
  uint32 maxUtilizations = uint32(DECIMALS + (DECIMALS << 16));
  for (uint256 j = 0; j < positionBalanceArray.length; j++) {
    positionBalanceArray[j] = PositionBalanceLibrary.storeBalanceData(
      positionBalanceArray[j].positionSize(),
      maxUtilizations,
      0
    );
  }
}
```
Also consider making `_validatePositionList` order-dependent if any logic depends on list ordering, or explicitly sorting the list before processing.

